        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Eryops megacephalus Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 127 µm (Cisuralian, 295 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 90.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 overall 90.8/100, superseding the Pass-1 audit at 84.3. The published GIF is the bone-masked composite (cv_sim_similarity 96.0, 12 frames, 720x540). Dispersion Pearson r is 0.99999998. Specimen metrics are not copies of their references (foreground 0.3208 vs 0.5, aspect 1.3358 vs 1, coherency 0.5334 vs 0.25). Overall 90.8/100 (faithfulness 90.7, reproducibility 91.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b44ba50e2b3311d637a471cbc44dcd63f77d40d0; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 93, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 89, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/eryops_megacephalus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0.py at b44ba50e2b3311d637a471cbc44dcd63f77d40d0, image/png, 561307 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 d39dec86b338897995a18611862cadc4735a89af83918444aa57064f98033d30 (sha256 d39dec86b338897995a18611862cadc4735a89af83918444aa57064f98033d30), spec_fingerprint 51cd1fdffca7c86caa7bb398d56aaa419b30f1491ad7e8b4fe11b7153e0b9b21. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 51cd1fdffca7c86caa7bb398d56aaa419b30f1491ad7e8b4fe11b7153e0b9b21; artifact_sha256: d39dec86b338897995a18611862cadc4735a89af83918444aa57064f98033d30; input_dataset_sha256: {eryops_megacephalus_amnh_specimen.jpg=11fc4e4eec64d5f1...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: reaction-diffusion instabilities select a finite critical wavenumber k_c. | Schnakenberg 1979: the quadratic two-species system used as the kinetics. | Pawley and Warren 2006: Eryops megacephalus Cope, 1877 is an Early Permian eryopoid; this slot uses 295 Ma. | Witzmann et al. 2010: basal tetrapod dermal bone carries sculptured ornament.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian and k_c with D scaled so lambda_c = 12 px = 127 µm on a 1.016 mm periodic patch. | Euler growth rates versus the discrete Laplacian symbol on modes m=2..16: Pearson r = 0.99999998, RMSE = 1.137e-4, KS = 0.0667. | Equal-diffusion control (max sigma = -0.4166, std 0.0399 to ~0) and autocatalysis ablation (std 0.0399 to 9.7e-5). | Otsu bone mask (foreground fraction 0.3208, aspect 1.3358) and a 12-frame 720x540 GIF. Masked cv_sim_similarity = 96.0, up from unmasked 94.4. Interior field Pearson r = 0.9913.; transfer_boundary: The 127 µm wavelength is the model scale. The AMNH photograph is an identity and silhouette standard, not a micrograph of dermal pits. | 8184 = 64*127+56 is the comparison to the organ-scale pit, not a second measurement of this fossil.; does_not_claim: Histological pit counts at 127 µm on this mount. | A successor Eryops chronospecies. Series length is 1. | That the nonlinear FFT peak equaling 127.0 µm is independent of the linear design mode. It is not.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=2.2]: Measure dermal-pit spacing on Eryops bone at a scale this gallery photograph cannot resolve.",
        "remediation needed: A histological measurement of dermal-pit spacing on Eryops bone, at a scale the AMNH gallery photograph cannot resolve, is still open." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.08e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Eryops megacephalus Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 127 µm (Cisuralian, 295 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Raising D_v/D_u from 20 to 80 shortens the reference wavelength at every step (4.013, 3.942, 3.908, 3.888, 3.870, 3.859). Equal diffusion drops max sigma to -0.4166 and the field standard deviation from 0.0399 to numerical noise. Removing autocatalysis drops the same initial standard deviation to 9.7e-5. Frame alpha runs from 0 to 0.40." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

