    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Eryops megacephalus Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 127 µm (Cisuralian, 295 Ma) (Eryops megacephalus)",
        "Eryops megacephalus Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 127 µm (Cisuralian, 295 Ma) faithfully reproduces Eryops megacephalus morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Eryops megacephalus specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Eryops megacephalus" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A successor Eryops chronospecies. Series length is 1.",
        "does_not_claim: Histological pit counts at 127 µm on this mount.",
        "does_not_claim: That the nonlinear FFT peak equaling 127.0 µm is independent of the linear design mode. It is not.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Equal-diffusion control (max sigma = -0.4166, std 0.0399 to ~0) and autocatalysis ablation (std 0.0399 to 9.7e-5).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Euler growth rates versus the discrete Laplacian symbol on modes m=2..16: Pearson r = 0.99999998, RMSE = 1.137e-4, KS = 0.0667.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian and k_c with D scaled so lambda_c = 12 px = 127 µm on a 1.016 mm periodic patch.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Otsu bone mask (foreground fraction 0.3208, aspect 1.3358) and a 12-frame 720x540 GIF. Masked cv_sim_similarity = 96.0, up from unmasked 94.4. Interior field Pearson r = 0.9913.",
        "reported_in_source: Pawley and Warren 2006: Eryops megacephalus Cope, 1877 is an Early Permian eryopoid; this slot uses 295 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the quadratic two-species system used as the kinetics.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: reaction-diffusion instabilities select a finite critical wavenumber k_c.",
        "reported_in_source: Witzmann et al. 2010: basal tetrapod dermal bone carries sculptured ornament.",
        "transfer_boundary: 8184 = 64*127+56 is the comparison to the organ-scale pit, not a second measurement of this fossil.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 127 µm wavelength is the model scale. The AMNH photograph is an identity and silhouette standard, not a micrograph of dermal pits." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Eryops megacephalus (Early Permian (Cisuralian, 295 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Amphibia & Reptilia (Ootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Eryops" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/eryops_megacephalus_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Eryops megacephalus; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952: reaction-diffusion instabilities select a finite critical wavenumber k_c. | Schnakenberg 1979: the quadratic two-species system used as the kinetics. | Pawley and Warren 2006: Eryops megacephalus Cope, 1877 is an Early Permian eryopoid; this slot uses 295 Ma. | Witzmann et al. 2010: basal tetrapod dermal bone carries sculptured ornament.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian and k_c with D scaled so lambda_c = 12 px = 127 µm on a 1.016 mm periodic patch. | Euler growth rates versus the discrete Laplacian symbol on modes m=2..16: Pearson r = 0.99999998, RMSE = 1.137e-4, KS = 0.0667. | Equal-diffusion control (max sigma = -0.4166, std 0.0399 to ~0) and autocatalysis ablation (std 0.0399 to 9.7e-5). | Otsu bone mask (foreground fraction 0.3208, aspect 1.3358) and a 12-frame 720x540 GIF. Masked cv_sim_similarity = 96.0, up from unmasked 94.4. Interior field Pearson r = 0.9913.; transfer_boundary: The 127 µm wavelength is the model scale. The AMNH photograph is an identity and silhouette standard, not a micrograph of dermal pits. | 8184 = 64*127+56 is the comparison to the organ-scale pit, not a second measurement of this fossil.; does_not_claim: Histological pit counts at 127 µm on this mount. | A successor Eryops chronospecies. Series length is 1. | That the nonlinear FFT peak equaling 127.0 µm is independent of the linear design mode. It is not.]; other sources: Eryops megacephalus skeleton at the American Museum of Natural History <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Eryops_megacephalus_skeleton_at_American_Museum_of_Natural_History.jpg>; phenomenon_size: 164 µm (0.0001637 m, log10=-3.786 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 164 µm to 36.8 cm): 164 µm:eryops-megacephalus-bioelectric-polarity, 512 µm:eryops-megacephalus-vertex-packing, 8.2 mm:eryops-megacephalus-turing-wavelength, 1.6 cm:eryops-megacephalus-clock-wavefront, 3.7 cm:eryops-megacephalus-morphogen-condensation, 4.5 cm:eryops-megacephalus-elastic-buckling, 5.1 cm:eryops-megacephalus-flux-canalization, 7.2 cm:eryops-megacephalus-branching-tree" ;
